# Environment Variables Configuration

# This is a template file. Copy this to `.env.local` and fill in your actual values.
# Never commit the actual .env.local file to version control!

# =============================================================================
# SUPABASE CONFIGURATION
# =============================================================================
# Get these from: https://supabase.com/dashboard/project/YOUR_PROJECT_ID/settings/api

# Your Supabase project URL
# Example: https://xxxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=your_supabase_project_url_here

# Your Supabase anonymous/public key (safe to use in client-side code)
# This is the 'anon' or 'public' key from your project settings
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key_here

# =============================================================================
# NOTES
# =============================================================================
# 
# 1. The VITE_ prefix is required for Vite to expose these variables to the client
# 2. Never commit your actual .env.local file to Git
# 3. The .env.local file is already in .gitignore
# 4. For production deployment, set these variables in your hosting platform
#    (Vercel, Netlify, etc.)
# 
# =============================================================================
# GETTING YOUR CREDENTIALS
# =============================================================================
# 
# 1. Go to https://supabase.com/dashboard
# 2. Select your project
# 3. Navigate to: Project Settings → API
# 4. Copy:
#    - Project URL → Use as VITE_SUPABASE_URL
#    - anon/public key → Use as VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
# 
# =============================================================================
# EDGE FUNCTIONS (Backend)
# =============================================================================
# 
# If you're deploying Edge Functions, you'll also need to set these as
# secrets in your Supabase project (not in this file):
# 
# SUPABASE_URL - Your project URL
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY - Your service role key (KEEP THIS SECRET!)
# 
# Set these using:
# supabase secrets set SUPABASE_URL=your_url
# supabase secrets set SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your_service_role_key
# 
# Or through the Supabase dashboard:
# Project Settings → Edge Functions → Secrets
# 
